The only times I've used show original was to see the complete
set of headers, e.g. to find out whether an approval was forged
in a moderated group.

Most of my participation in newsgroups is in programming
newsgroups, where the correct presentation of code extracts is
essential.  I've not found this to be a problem with Google.

>   Truncating messages.  Encouraging users to think Usenet is
>   for those with short attention spans, like irc.

>   No automatic spell checking(?).  It wouldn't be perfect, but
